-- title:
--   Pole chart ring spanned by reductions of the integral chart algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $p$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid p$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ has characteristic $\ell$. Let $\mathrm{fm}$ be a `CharPModel.FibreModel` for level $p$ over $A$ with residue characteristic $\ell$, coefficient field $k$ and reduction map the residue homomorphism $A \to k$; in particular it provides two subrings $B_{\mathrm{Fin}}, B_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ of `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull p)` together with ring homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{Fin}}, \pi_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ into `modularFunctionFieldC k p`, the subfield of $k((q))$ generated over $k$ by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k p`. Assume moreover that for every $b$ in the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra `chartAlgInf p ℓ` $=$ `chartAlg p ℓ {(jFull p)⁻¹}` of `modularFunctionFieldFull p`, the element obtained from $b$ by applying the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb` into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, regarded inside `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull p)`, lies in $\mathrm{fm}.B_{\mathrm{Inf}}$. The conclusion is that every $z \in$ `modularFunctionFieldC k p` which is integral over the $k$-subalgebra generated by $(\mathrm{jqModC}\,k)^{-1}$ — that is, lies in `CurveModel.chartRing k {(jqModC k)⁻¹}` — can be written as a finite sum $z = \sum_{i<n} c_i\, \pi_{\mathrm{Inf}}(b_i)$ for some $n$, scalars $c_i \in k$ (pushed into `modularFunctionFieldC k p` along the structure map) and elements $b_i$ of `chartAlgInf p ℓ`, each $b_i$ being fed to $\pi_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ through the membership supplied by the hypothesis.
--
--   This is the ring-level surjectivity statement at the pole chart $1/j$ for the special fibre of the Igusa model: the characteristic-$\ell$ chart ring is already spanned over the residue field by the reductions of the integral chart algebra, which reflects the normality of the special fibre. It is the pole-chart counterpart of the corresponding statement at the finite chart, and is used in comparing places of the characteristic-$\ell$ modular function field with those coming from the fibre model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_piInf_image_spans_chartAlg.lean

